   "h": "Questions engineers ask",
   "items": [
    {
     "q": "Single-pass or double-pass RO?",
     "a": "Single-pass RO and EDI suits moderate solids. Double pass adds margin on conductivity, TOC and silica, for high-solids feed or PW feeding a WFI still or pure steam generator."
    },
    {
     "q": "How do you handle cold winter feed?",
     "a": "Rated at 25 °C, RO can lose a third or more of its output at 5 °C. We size at your coldest feed, or add a heat exchanger."
    },
    {
     "q": "Our supply is chloraminated. What changes?",
     "a": "Chloramine damages RO membranes, so it is removed first, which releases ammonia. Ammonia can pass RO when pH is raised for CO₂ control, so we design both together."
    },
    {
     "q": "Hot water or chemical sanitization?",
     "a": "Hot water leaves no residual to test for and is proven at the coldest point. Chemical sanitization suits membranes not rated for heat, but adds a residual test."
    },
    {
     "q": "How do we know it will pass IQ/OQ?",
     "a": "Your quality unit approves the FAT protocol and witnesses a wet FAT, in person or remotely, before the skid ships. SAT and OQ then prove performance on your feed."
    }
   ],
